/* ===================== *
 *    Phantom Thief      *
 * ===================== */
@901 = ~phantom~
@902 = ~Phantom Thief~
@903 = ~Phantom Thief:

A supernatural assassin who combines conventional thievery with spectral powers. Phantom Thieves channel ethereal energy into their ambushes, striking through magical defenses that stop ordinary assassination techniques.

Advantages:
- Phantom Ambush (passive): The Phantom Thief has no backstab damage multiplier. Instead, the first attack made from stealth or invisibility with a thief backstab weapon deals additional magic damage, regardless of the target's angle:
  1st level: +2d6
  5th level: +3d6
  9th level: +4d6
  13th level: +5d6
  17th level: +6d6
  The bonus damage is not multiplied by critical hits, bypasses Protection from Magical Weapons, Stoneskin, Mantle and Improved Mantle, and works on creatures immune to backstabbing. It remains subject to magic resistance and magic damage resistance.
- Phantom Veil: Become invisible for 3 rounds. Movement does not break the invisibility; attacking does. 1 use per day at 1st level, plus 1 additional use every 4 levels thereafter.
- Phantom Fear (9th level): Unleash a terrifying spectral presence that frightens nearby enemies and halves their movement speed for 3 rounds. Save vs. spell negates. 1 use per day at 9th level, plus 1 additional use every 5 levels thereafter.
- High-Level Ability: Phantom Execution replaces Assassination.

Disadvantages:
- No normal backstab multiplier.
- Cannot set traps: the Set Spike Trap, Set Explosive Trap and Set Time Trap high-level abilities are not available.~
@904 = ~Phantom Ambush~
@905 = ~Phantom Ambush

The Phantom Thief replaces the conventional backstab with a supernatural assassination technique. The first attack made from stealth or invisibility with a thief backstab weapon deals additional magic damage:

1st level: +2d6
5th level: +3d6
9th level: +4d6
13th level: +5d6
17th level: +6d6

This damage ignores the target's angle, is not multiplied by critical hits, bypasses Protection from Magical Weapons, Stoneskin, Mantle and Improved Mantle, and affects creatures that are normally immune to backstabbing. It is subject to magic resistance and magic damage resistance. Once the Phantom Thief has been revealed, no further Phantom Ambush is possible until stealth is regained.~
@906 = ~Phantom Veil~
@907 = ~Phantom Veil

Wrapping <PRO_HIMHER>self in spectral energy, the Phantom Thief becomes invisible for 3 rounds. Moving does not break the invisibility; attacking does, and a Phantom Ambush can be delivered from it.

Uses: 1 per day, plus 1 additional use every 4 levels after 1st.~
@908 = ~Phantom Fear~
@909 = ~Phantom Fear

The Phantom Thief unleashes a terrifying spectral presence. Every enemy within 20 feet must save vs. spell or be struck by fear and have its movement speed halved for 3 rounds.

Uses: 1 per day at 9th level, plus 1 additional use every 5 levels thereafter.~
@910 = ~Phantom Execution~
@911 = ~Phantom Execution

Empowers the Phantom Thief's next Phantom Ambush (it lasts up to one turn). The Ambush deals an additional 10d6 magic damage and stuns the target for 1 round. The target may save vs. death at -2 to avoid the stun. The additional damage is subject to magic resistance and magic damage resistance.~
@912 = ~Phantom Ambush!~
@913 = ~Phantom Veil~
@914 = ~Phantom Fear~
@915 = ~Phantom Execution~
